      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $Y$ be an arbitrary object of $\calX $, we wish to show that composition with $f$ induces a $(-1)$-truncated map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calX }( Y, \emptyset ) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calX }(Y, X). \]
</div>
    <p>
       If $Y$ is an initial object of $\calX $, then both sides are contractible; otherwise the left side is empty (Lemma <a href="/tag/0FD9C4" data-tag="0FD9C4">6.1.3.6</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
